course: dictionary
lesson: 8732
title: Serfs and the land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clues in a sentence can tell you what a word means. «Serfs were farmers tied to a landlord's land who could not leave freely.» The clues are farmers, tied, land and could not leave, and they tell you what a serf was.
explain: Serf is a noun, so it names a person. Serfs is the plural, meaning more than one serf. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence: a serf was a farmer who had to stay on the lord's land. If that makes sense, your meaning fits.
explain: A serf was not a slave, because a serf could not be sold alone. But a serf was not free either, because he could not leave the land. «Taras Shevchenko (1814–1861) was born a serf» shows that a person could be born into this life.
fact: A serf was a farm worker who lived and worked on a lord's land and could not leave it.
fact: Serfs gave the lord part of their crops and some days of work.
fact: Serfs were not slaves, because they could not be sold alone, but they were not free.
fact: Serfs lived in the Middle Ages in Europe and Russia.
fact: Serfdom ended in the Austrian Empire in 1848 and in the Russian Empire, including much of Ukraine, in 1861.
exercise: «Serfs, farmers tied to a landlord's land, were freed in the Russian Empire, including much of Ukraine, only in 1861.» What does tied to a landlord's land mean? | Owned a big ship | Were always rich | Could move wherever they liked | *Had to stay on the landlord's land
exercise: «Serfs were not slaves, because they could not be sold alone.» Why were serfs not slaves? | *They could not be sold on their own | They could leave whenever they wanted | They were paid a lot of money | They were the lord's children
exercise: «Taras Shevchenko was born a serf and became Ukraine's national poet.» What does born a serf mean? | He was born on a ship | He was born in a castle | *He was a serf from the day he was born | He was born in the year 1861
test: Which is true about serfs in the Middle Ages? | Serfs were always free to move away | Serfs were the lords who ruled the castle | Serfs owned the land they farmed | *Serfs could not leave the land freely
test: «Serfdom ended in the Russian Empire, including much of Ukraine, in 1861.» In which year did serfdom end there? | 1783 | *1861 | 1838 | 1848
exam: Why were serfs not slaves, even though they were not free? | They were paid wages in gold | They owned the lord's castle | *They could not be sold on their own | They could go anywhere they wanted
